  "id": "chandelier-room",
  "name": "Chandelier room",
  "description": "Grey-box room for hanging things that fall (mw-e03.13). West: an iron chandelier hangs from a hemp rope under a beam, over the spot at x -4; stand under it, then shoot or burn the rope and the chandelier drops on whoever is there (a frayed rope: 20 hp, and a pierce hit has to be 29 or more to get through its 30% resistance, so a half-drawn arrow only frays it). East: a rope bridge of twelve planks between two stone platforms, rated for 150 kg, with a 160 kg anvil hanging from its own rope over the middle; cut the anvil's rope and the weight snaps the bridge's weaker rope, which takes the whole span down. A knight crossing it weighs next to nothing. Reach it with ?scene=chandelier-room; the beams are floating stand-ins for a ceiling, and the two hanging ropes are a chunky 16 cm so a bow can find them from across the room.",
